Read docs/CRYPTO_V8_NEWS_TRUTH_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task. Doctrine recap: TRUTH — honest empty beats stale/cross-contaminated news, NEVER show another asset's articles, filtered-to-zero renders the spec's empty copy in existing empty-state styling. NO new serverless files — all server edits in api/news.ts only (Hobby 12-function cap), no new npm deps, vercel.json keeps fra1. Params additive-only: bare /api/news?q= legacy behavior unchanged; TN path (region=tn) completely untouched by horizon/match/sort changes. Keyless only; curl-verify when:7d behavior from prod before coding. Verify per task: market-ui typecheck 0 + vercel --prod (repo root — apps/market-ui path breaks the project link) + prod curl real numbers + audit green (spot 200/200, MISMATCH 0) + TN news regression (BIAT still Ilboursa-class) + cross-contamination spot-check (VELO and GRAM panels: zero generic-Bitcoin titles). Flip the task to [x], append one Progress-log line with real numbers, commit on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). PERSISTENCE: never end the loop because of a usage/rate limit, 429, or overloaded error — on any such error stop consuming tokens, ScheduleWakeup at 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log are recovery state; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations); chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining, or a task blocked on something only the user can provide — then say exactly what's needed and still ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes if supplied.
